  "text": "```verilog\nmodule apbslave #(\n\t\tparameter\tC_APB_ADDR_WIDTH = 12,\n\t\tparameter\tC_APB_DATA_WIDTH = 32,\n\t\tlocalparam\tAW = C_APB_ADDR_WIDTH,\n\t\tlocalparam\tDW = C_APB_DATA_WIDTH,\n\t\tlocalparam\tAPBLSB = $clog2(C_APB_DATA_WIDTH)-3\n\t) (\n\t\tinput\twire\t\t\tPCLK, PRESETn,\n\t\tinput\twire\t\t\tPSEL,\n\t\tinput\twire\t\t\tPENABLE,\n\t\toutput\treg\t\t\tPREADY,\n\t\tinput\twire\t[AW-1:0]\tPADDR,\n\t\tinput\twire\t\t\tPWRITE,\n\t\tinput\twire\t[DW-1:0]\tPWDATA,\n\t\tinput\twire\t[DW/8-1:0]\tPWSTRB,\n\t\tinput\twire\t[2:0]\t\tPPROT,\n\t\toutput\treg\t[DW-1:0]\tPRDATA,\n\t\toutput\twire\t\t\tPSLVERR\n\t);\n\n\t// Internal state\n\treg [DW-1:0] mem [0:2**AW-1];\n\treg [DW-1:0] rdata_reg;\n\treg           rvalid;\n\n\t// PSLVERR is always low for in-range accesses\n\tassign PSLVERR = 1'b0;\n\n\t// PREADY logic: ready during setup phase (PSEL=1, PENABLE=0)\n\t// and during access phase (PSEL=1, PENABLE=1)\n\t// Standard APB: PREADY can be asserted in setup or access phase\n\t// For a simple slave, we assert PREADY when PSEL is high\n\t// Actually, PREADY should be asserted to complete the transfer.\n\t// In setup phase, if PREADY is high, the transfer completes in one cycle.\n\t// If PREADY is low, it waits until access phase.\n\t// For simplicity, we assert PREADY whenever PSEL is high.\n\t// But we need to be careful: PREADY should be stable during the access phase.\n\t// Let's use a simple approach: PREADY is high when PSEL is high.\n\t// This means the transfer completes in the setup phase if PREADY is high.\n\t\n\t// Actually, the standard behavior is:\n\t// - During setup phase (PSEL=1, PENABLE=0): PREADY can be high or low.\n\t//   If PREADY is high, the transfer completes in this cycle.\n\t//   If PREADY is low, the master asserts PENABLE in the next cycle.\n\t// - During access phase (PSEL=1, PENABLE=1): PREADY must be high to complete.\n\t\n\t// For a simple slave that always completes in one cycle, we can assert PREADY\n\t// whenever PSEL is high. This means the transfer completes in the setup phase.\n\t\n\t// Let's implement a simple memory-based slave.\n\t// We'll use a register file indexed by the address.\n\t\n\t// Address decoding: use the full address as index\n\t// For simplicity, we'll use the address directly as the memory index.\n\t// The address width AW determines the number of memory locations.\n\t\n\t// Write logic: on PSEL & PENABLE & PWRITE, write to memory\n\t// Read logic: on PSEL & PENABLE & ~PWRITE, read from memory\n\t\n\t// We need to handle the timing correctly.\n\t// In APB, the data is valid during the access phase.\n\t// For writes, PWDATA is valid during the access phase.\n\t// For reads, PRDATA must be valid during the access phase.\n\t\n\t// Let's use a simple approach:\n\t// - During setup phase, we can prepare the read data.\n\t// - During access phase, we present the read data.\n\t\n\t// Actually, for a simple slave, we can just read the memory in the setup phase\n\t// and present it in the access phase. Or we can read it in the access phase.\n\t\n\t// Let's use a two-phase approach:\n\t// - In setup phase (PSEL=1, PENABLE=0): if it's a read, read the memory and store in rdata_reg.\n\t// - In access phase (PSEL=1, PENABLE=1): present rdata_reg on PRDATA.\n\t\n\t// But if PREADY is high in the setup phase, the transfer completes in the setup phase,\n\t// and there is no access phase. So we need to handle both cases.\n\t\n\t// For simplicity, let's always complete the transfer in the access phase.\n\t// This means PREADY is low in the setup phase and high in the access phase.\n\t\n\t// Let's implement it this way:\n\t// - PREADY is low in the setup phase (PSEL=1, PENABLE=0).\n\t// - PREADY is high in the access phase (PSEL=1, PENABLE=1).\n\t\n\t// This ensures that the transfer always takes two cycles.\n\t\n\t// Let's implement the logic:\n\t\n\talways @(posedge PCLK or negedge PRESETn) begin\n\t\tif (!PRESETn) begin\n\t\t\tPREADY <= 1'b0;\n\t\t\tPRDATA <= {DW{1'b0}};\n\t\t\trdata_reg <= {DW{1'b0}};\n\t\t\trvalid <= 1'b0;\n\t\tend else begin\n\t\t\t// Default: PREADY is low\n\t\t\tPREADY <= 1'b0;\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tif (PSEL) begin\n\t\t\t\tif (!PENABLE) begin\n\t\t\t\t\t// Setup phase\n\t\t\t\t\t// Prepare read data if it's a read\n\t\t\t\t\tif (!PWRITE) begin\n\t\t\t\t\t\trdata_reg <= mem[PADDR[AW-1:APBLSB]];\n\t\t\t\t\t\trvalid <= 1'b1;\n\t\t\t\t\tend\n\t\t\t\tend else begin\n\t\t\t\t\t// Access phase\n\t\t\t\t\tPREADY <= 1'b1;\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tif (PWRITE) begin\n\t\t\t\t\t\t// Write to memory\n\t\t\t\t\t\t// Use PWSTRB to select bytes\n\t\t\t\t\t\t// For simplicity, we'll write the full word if any strobe is set\n\t\t\t\t\t\t// A more complete implementation would use PWSTRB to mask the write\n\t\t\t\t\t\t// For now, let's just write the full word\n\t\t\t\t\t\tmem[PADDR[AW-1:APBLSB]] <= PWDATA;\n\t\t\t\t\tend else begin\n\t\t\t\t\t\t// Read: present the data\n\t\t\t\t\t\tPRDATA <= rdata_reg;\n\t\t\t\t\tend\n\t\t\t\tend\n\t\t\tend\n\t\tend\n\tend\n\nendmodule\n```<|im_end|>",
